### IPP-1005 Backup export / import tests
### Put ADMIN_PASSWORD from server/.env while testing, then put CHANGE_ME back

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@adminEmail = askedin143@gmail.com
@adminPassword = CHANGE_ME
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.data.token}}


### 1. Admin login -> expect 200
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }


### 2. Export -> expect 200, data.backup with languages (topics) and questions
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/backup/export
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 3. Dry run (nothing is saved) -> expect 1 to add, 1 skipped with "MCQ must have exactly 4 options"
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/backup/import?dryRun=true
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "questions": [
    { "language": "php", "type": "qa", "topic": "oop", "question": "TEST (IPP-1005): what is a constructor?", "answer": "A method that runs when an object is created." },
    { "language": "php", "type": "mcq", "topic": "oop", "question": "TEST bad mcq", "answer": "x", "options": ["a", "b"], "correctOption": 0 }
  ]
}


### 4. Not a backup -> expect 400 "This does not look like a backup file..."
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/backup/import?dryRun=true
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "hello": "world" }
